  "note": "How the mockup of the OpenZone window in VPP (docs/specs/2026-11-12-openzone-vpp-mockup/project, HTML and CSS) becomes the window's layouts: `python -m dayz_mcp.css2layout ui/css2layout.json [page] [--demo]` from the MCP repository's src. This file holds what the whole series shares -- the fonts of the window (Fira Sans and Fira Sans Condensed as the ozv_* atlases of OpenZone_VPP/gui/fonts), the characters those faces lack (drawn as icons of the ozv_ui imageset) and the icons -- and the core's own pages. A glue's ui/css2layout.json extends this one and names its pages, its output folder and its stringtable. The sizes are the 'exact text size' that draws a CSS pixel size as the browser does (measured: the cell is 1.11 to 1.15 of the em).",
